{"strongs": "H3547", "word": "כָּהַן", "translit": "ka.han", "root": "כהן", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "act as priest", "definition": "II. [ כָּהַן ] verb only Pi`el denominative act as priest ; — Perfect כִּהֵן Exod 40:13 ; 1Chr 5:36 3 masculine plural כִּהֲנוּ Exod 28:41 ; Exod 40:15 Imperfect 3 masculine singular יְכַהֵן Num 3:4 + 2 t.; plural יְכַהֲנוּ 1Chr 24:2 Infinitive construct כַּהֵן Exod 29:1 + 11 t.; suffix כַּהֲנוֺ Exod 28:1 ; Exod 28:3 ; Exod 28:4 . — 1. minister as a priest , absolute Exod 31:10 ; Exod 35:19 ; Exod 39:41 ; Lev 16:32 ; Num 3:3 ; Num 3:4 (all P ); לִי ׳ כ minister to me ( ׳ י ) Exod 28:1 ; Exod 28:3 ; Exod 28:4 ; Exod 28:41 ; Exod 29:1 ; Exod 29:44 ; Exod 30:30 ; Exod 40:13 ; Exod 40:15 (all P ), Ezek 44:13 ; Hos 4:6 ליהוה ׳ כ Lev 7:35 ( P ), 1Chr 5:36 ; 1Chr 24:2 ; 2Chr 11:14 (always of Aaron and his sons, except Ezek 44:13 ; 2Chr 11:14 , where Levites are forbidden to minister; and Hos 4:6 of Israel, whose national priesthood is taken away). 2. be or become priest Deut 10:6 ( E ?). 3. play the priest: כֶּחָתָן יְכַהֵן פְּאֵר Isa 61:10 as a bridegroom ( that ) priests it with his turban , decks himself with a splendid turban such as the priests wore.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3932')\">BDB3932</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3547')\">H3547</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3931')\">BDB3931</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3933')\">BDB3933</entry></div><p> II. [<bdbheb>כָּהַן</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> only <b>Pi`el denominative</b> <highlightword>act as priest</highlightword>; — <highlight>Perfect</highlight> <bdbheb>כִּהֵן</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 40:13\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(2,40,13)\">Exod 40:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Chr 5:36\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(13,5,36)\">1Chr 5:36</ref> 3 masculine plural <bdbheb>כִּהֲנוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 28:41\" b=\"